 pregnancy: a matter of 'equity and common sense'</article-title><source>Guttmacher Policy Review</source><year>2006</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>2</fpage><lpage>7</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hwang</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Grimes</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Shields</surname><given-names>WC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Universal insurance coverage for contraceptives: a public health imperative</article-title><source>Contraception</source><year>2004</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>357</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15504372</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.contraception.2004.08.001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Burdette</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Rodriguez</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Looking inward: provider-based barriers to contraception among teens and young adults</article-title><source>Contraception</source><year>2008</year><volume>78</volume><fpage>355</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18929730</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.contraception.2008.07.021</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ranjit</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Bankole</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Darroch</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Contraceptive failure in the first two years of use: differences across socioeconomic subgroups</article-title><source>Fam Plann P